                <pb facs="0441" n="429" sameAs="frus:frus1945v06/pg429"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">195.7 <hi rendition="#italic">Jean
                    Nicolet</hi>/5–2645: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bern</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-05-26">May 26,
                        1945</date>.<lb/>[Received May 26—11 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2920. Am[erican] Interests—Japan. Department’s 4184, December 12.<anchor n="10"
                        xml:id="d304-f1"/> Swiss note May 25 gives in translation following Japanese
                    reply telegraphed May 24 by Swiss Legation, Tokyo: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Serious investigations made by competent authorities were unable
                            disclose any act corresponding similar accident. Japanese Government
                            takes occasion reaffirm that all Japanese warships, boats and vessels
                            strictly observe laws of war.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harrison</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
